Usage: taskpush [global flags] <command> [command flags]

Commands:
  send      send one notification
  finish    send the timed result and clean up the state
  start     record the start of a timed run
  check     validate channels without sending
  list      list configured channels
  types     list channel types or their fields
  init      write a minimal configuration
  version   print the version
  help      print help

Global flags:
  --help, -h                   show help, and after a command show that command's help
  --version                    show the version
  --lang LANG                  output language: en or zh-CN, default en

Configuration mode: --config, TASKPUSH_CONFIG_JSON or ./taskpush.json supplies the channels
Inline mode: --webhook, --type, --set or --payload builds one channel and ignores TASKPUSH_CONFIG_JSON
Flags may appear before or after the command; everything after -- is a positional argument; --help after a command shows that command's help

Examples:
  taskpush check --config taskpush.json
  taskpush send --config taskpush.json --title example
  taskpush send --webhook https://example.com/hook --payload {}

See docs/usage.md and docs/taskpush.example.json
